---
/*
  LOGO COMPONENT — real PYT logo (2026-08-18, sized-variant added
  2026-08-19, precise crop-alignment added 2026-08-19).

  The logo graphic itself contains BOTH the colored "PYT" mark and the
  "Peninsula Youth Theatre" wordmark stacked underneath, with a row of
  decorative stars ABOVE the "PYT" letters — so there is no separate
  HTML text next to it anymore (there used to be; removed on purpose
  to avoid showing the name twice).

  Two sizes:
   - size="nav" (default) — small, used in the header on every page
     EXCEPT the homepage. Simple: scales the whole image (including
     the decorative stars) to a fixed height. No special alignment
     needed here, it just needs to look like a normal logo mark.
   - size="hero" — bigger, used once on the homepage, sitting next to
     (desktop) or above (mobile) the hero headline. This one uses a
     precise crop/offset so the TOP OF THE "PYT" LETTERS (not the
     decorative stars above them) lines up with the top of the
     headline text, and the BOTTOM OF THE "PENINSULA YOUTH THEATRE"
     WORDMARK lines up with the bottom of the headline text — the
     decorative stars are allowed to poke up above that aligned box,
     same as they do in the source artwork.

     The crop percentages below (26.47% / 97.50%) were measured
     directly from the actual image file's pixel rows (not eyeballed)
     — see BUILD_LOG.md for how. If the logo artwork is ever replaced
     with a different file, these percentages will need remeasuring.

  Every page uses THIS component, so swapping the file here updates
  the logo everywhere at once, at both sizes.

  TWO DIFFERENT FILES (2026-09-21):
   - size="nav" uses /uploads/pyt-logo-transparent.png — a TRANSPARENT
     version, because the header and footer are pale teal under the
     duotone scheme and the original file's white background showed as
     a white box. "nav" size covers the header on every page except the
     homepage, and the footer on EVERY page (the homepage included).
     The PM's transparent file had a pale rim left over from removing
     its white background (4-10px wide — the file had been enlarged
     from a smaller original). The rim was removed by un-mixing the
     white out of each edge pixel, and the file resized to 600px wide
     (it had been 1125px / 393KB for a logo shown ~100px wide). If a
     new transparent logo is supplied, check its edges on teal first.
   - size="hero" (homepage, on white) still uses the ORIGINAL
     /uploads/pyt-logo-stars.png, deliberately: its crop/offset numbers
     below were measured from that exact file, and it sits on white.

  The transparent file is cropped TIGHTER than the original, so at the
  same height its letters would look ~6% bigger. Its heights (42px /
  51px, against the original's 44px / 54px) were calculated so the
  visible PYT letters + wordmark are the SAME size as before — the
  header width changes by under 2px. If you swap this file, re-measure.
*/
interface Props {
  size?: "nav" | "hero";
  /* MARK ONLY (2026-09-22, PM request: "look how Apple's logo and nav
     items are uniform"). The header shows just the "PYT" letters,
     cropped out of the same file — no wordmark, no stars — so the logo
     reads as one more item in the menu rather than a different kind of
     object. The FOOTER keeps the full lockup, wordmark and all, which
     is why this is a prop rather than a change to the nav size. */
  mark?: boolean;
}
const { size = "nav", mark = false } = Astro.props;
---

{size === "hero" ? (
  <a href="/" class="logo logo-hero" aria-label="Peninsula Youth Theatre — home">
    <span class="logo-hero-frame">
      <img src="/uploads/pyt-logo-stars.png" alt="Peninsula Youth Theatre" class="logo-mark logo-mark-hero" width="2526" height="1398" />
    </span>
  </a>
) : (
  <a href="/" class={`logo logo-nav ${mark ? "logo-nav-mark" : ""}`} aria-label="Peninsula Youth Theatre — home">
    <span class="logo-nav-frame">
      <img src="/uploads/pyt-logo-transparent.png" alt="Peninsula Youth Theatre" class="logo-mark" width="600" height="309" />
    </span>
  </a>
)}

<style>
  .logo {
    /* Never let this shrink — without this, the logo's flex box could
       get squeezed narrower than its own image needs whenever the
       header ran low on space (mid-width screens, and mobile with
       Register/Donate/ES/hamburger all competing for room). Once
       squeezed, the site-wide "img { max-width: 100% }" reset (see
       global.css) would clamp the image's WIDTH to fit the shrunk
       box while its HEIGHT stayed locked at 44px/54px — that
       width/height mismatch is what visibly squashed/distorted it.
       This makes the logo's own box immovable, so that clamp never
       triggers. (PM report, 2026-08-19: "no home button... unless you
       squash the page down, and then a squashed logo appears.") */
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .logo-mark {
    height: var(--logo-h, 42px);   /* transparent file — see the TWO DIFFERENT FILES note */
    width: auto;
    display: block;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 520px) {
    .logo-nav .logo-mark {
      --logo-h: 51px;   /* transparent file — see the TWO DIFFERENT FILES note */
    }
  }

  /* MARK-ONLY CROP (2026-09-22) — the header version.
     Measured on the actual pixels of pyt-logo-transparent.png (600 x
     309): the big "PYT" letters occupy rows 62-238 and columns 51-557.
     The frame is a window of that size and the image is scaled up and
     shifted so only those letters show. Everything is expressed against
     --mark-h (the height of the visible letters), so changing that one
     number resizes the mark correctly:
       image height = 309/176 = 1.7557
       frame width  = 506/176 = 2.8750
       shift up     =  62/176 = 0.3523
       shift left   =  51/176 = 0.2898
     Because the crop starts exactly at the ink, the mark needs no
     alignment nudge: its left edge IS the letters' left edge.
     If the logo file is ever replaced, re-measure those four rows and
     columns. */
  .logo-nav-mark .logo-nav-frame {
    --mark-h: 20px;
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
    height: var(--mark-h);
    width: calc(var(--mark-h) * 2.875);
  }

  .logo-nav-mark .logo-mark {
    position: absolute;
    top: calc(var(--mark-h) * -0.3523);
    left: calc(var(--mark-h) * -0.2898);
    height: calc(var(--mark-h) * 1.7557);
    width: auto;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* LETTERS FLUSH WITH THE EDGE, NOT THE FILE (2026-09-22, PM request).
     The transparent logo file has decorative stars that stick out past
     the lettering: measured on the actual pixels, the "PYT"/wordmark ink
     starts 6.67% of the file's width in from the left and stops 3.50%
     short of the right. Lining the FILE up with the menu therefore left
     the letters looking indented. These negative margins pull the file
     out by exactly those amounts, so the LETTERS line up with whatever
     sits beside the logo. The numbers are the measured fractions times
     the file's aspect ratio (600 / 309 = 1.942), expressed against the
     logo's own height so they follow any size change:
       left  = 0.0667 x 1.942 = 0.1295
       right = 0.0350 x 1.942 = 0.0680
     The stars still show — nothing is cropped. If the logo FILE is ever
     replaced, re-measure these two fractions. */
  .logo-nav .logo-mark {
    margin-left: calc(var(--logo-h, 42px) * -0.1295);
    margin-right: calc(var(--logo-h, 42px) * -0.068);
  }

  /* Hero size: the frame is sized to exactly the headline text
     block's height (PYT-top to wordmark-bottom); the image itself is
     scaled bigger than that and shifted up inside it, so the stars
     above "PYT" poke out above the frame instead of being counted as
     part of the aligned height. Numbers recalculated 2026-08-19 for
     the switch to Baloo 2 at a bigger size with a tightened
     line-height (see index.astro) — if the headline font-size,
     line-height, or typeface changes again, these should be
     revisited together. */
  /* QUARTER SIZE (2026-09-22, PM request): every number in this block and
     the two below is exactly half what it was, so the crop and the
     offset still line up the same way — the stars poke above the frame
     and the wordmark sits on its bottom edge. Was 50 / 127.2 on phones
     and 87 / 221.3 on desktop. */
  .logo-hero-frame {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    overflow: visible;
    height: 12.5px;
    width: 31.8px;
  }

  .logo-mark-hero {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: -4.65px;
    height: 17.6px;
    width: auto;
  }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .logo-hero-frame {
      height: 21.8px;
      width: 55.3px;
    }

    .logo-mark-hero {
      top: -8.1px;
      height: 30.6px;
    }
  }
</style>
